      \field{abstract}{Let R be a commutative ring. One may ask when a general R -module P that satisfies \$P \textbackslash oplus R \textbackslash cong R\textasciicircum n\$ has a free summand of a given rank. M. Raynaud translated this question into one about sections of certain maps between Stiefel varieties: if \$V\_r(\textbackslash mathbb \textbraceleft A\textbraceright\textasciicircum n)\$ denotes the variety \$\textbackslash operatorname \textbraceleft GL\textbraceright (n) / \textbackslash operatorname \textbraceleft GL\textbraceright (n-r)\$ over a field k , then the projection \$V\_r(\textbackslash mathbb \textbraceleft A\textbraceright\textasciicircum n) \textbackslash to V\_1(\textbackslash mathbb \textbraceleft A\textbraceright\textasciicircum n)\$ has a section if and only if the following holds: any module P over any k -algebra R with the property that \$P \textbackslash oplus R \textbackslash cong R\textasciicircum n\$ has a free summand of rank \$r-1\$ . Using techniques from \$\textbackslash mathbb \textbraceleft A\textbraceright\textasciicircum 1\$ -homotopy theory, we characterize those n for which the map \$V\_r(\textbackslash mathbb \textbraceleft A\textbraceright\textasciicircum n) \textbackslash to V\_1(\textbackslash mathbb \textbraceleft A\textbraceright\textasciicircum n)\$ has a section in the cases \$r=3,4\$ under some assumptions on the base field. We conclude that if \$P \textbackslash oplus R \textbackslash cong R\textasciicircum\textbraceleft 24m\textbraceright\$ and R contains the field of rational numbers, then P contains a free summand of rank \$2\$ . If R contains a quadratically closed field of characteristic \$0\$ , or the field of real numbers, then P contains a free summand of rank \$3\$ . The analogous results hold for schemes and vector bundles over them.;Let R be a commutative ring. One may ask when a general R-module P that satisfies \$P \textbackslash oplus R \textbackslash cong R\textasciicircum n\$ has a free summand o