c {$H\infty$}-spectra. Using this, we show that the naive motivic analogue of the unstable Kahn-Priddy theorem fails. Over the complex numbers, we show that the motivic {$T$}-spectrum S [ {$\eta$} - 1 , {$\mu$} 9 - 1 ] is closely related to higher Witt groups, where {$S$} is the motivic sphere spectrum and {$H$} and {$\mu_9$} are explicit elements in {$\pi$}**({$S$}).;}
