      \field{abstract}{Let k be an algebraically closed field of characteristic zero. Let c:{$S\mathcal{H}\rightarrowS\mathcal{H}$}(k) be the functor induced by sending a space to the constant presheaf of spaces on Sm/k. We show that c is fully faithful. In consequence, c induces an isomorphism c*:{$\pi$}n(E){$\rightarrow\Pi$}n,0(c(E))(k) for all spectra E and all n{$\in\mathbb{Z}$}. Fix an embedding {$\sigma$}:k{$\rightarrow\mathbb{C}$} and let ReB:{$S\mathcal{H}$}(k){$\rightarrowS\mathcal{H}$} be the associated Betti realization. We show that the slice tower for the motivic sphere spectrum over k, {$\mathbb{S}$}k, has Betti realization which is strongly convergent. This gives a spectral sequence `of motivic origin' converging to the homotopy groups of the sphere spectrum {$\mathbb{S}\inS\mathcal{H}$}; this spectral sequence at E2 agrees with the E2 terms in the Adams--Novikov spectral sequence after a reindexing. Finally, we show that, for {$\varepsilon$} a torsion object in {$S\mathcal{H}$}(k)eff, the Betti realization induces an isomorphism {$\Pi$}n, 0({$\varepsilon$})(k){$\rightarrow\pi$}n(ReB{$\varepsilon$}) for all n, generalizing the Suslin--Voevodsky theorem comparing mod N Suslin homology and mod N singular homology.}
